## Capacity and remaining prerequisites

Operative lifetime file/PRE record capacities remain **32/32**. Full historical
HTTP paths need at least69 entries; original PRE needs53 records. Proposed96/PRE64
is **NOT_ADOPTED**, awaiting the single material Homeowner decision. Twenty families,
10MiB aggregate,16KiB metadata and no-refund physical-copy accounting remain fixed.
No truncation, record splitting or output dropping can manufacture full-path fit.

Preflight marker field `ABSENT_NOT_CONSUMED_THIS_BATCH` is fixed batch nonconsumption
metadata, not a fresh filesystem check of a configured future marker. Candidate has
no such marker path. Do not interpret it as live marker-absence/admission evidence.
Full-driver httpx/fastapi/redis dependency surface, actual XML/Alembic seams,
unexpected native output, live fixture/owned databases, physical SQL and Linux
cleanup remain unqualified. No installation or effect permission is inferred.

